E028: SCUMM v1-v2 in the bridge: the input and sentence scripts the engine runs, the sentence line and the inventory as
slots, actors in pixels

SCUMM v1-v2 (Maniac Mansion) have no VAR_VERB_SCRIPT and VAR_SENTENCE_SCRIPT (both 0xFF): the engine always runs global
4 for a click and global 2 for a sentence. The idle rule, the input log and the skips read them through
inputScript()/sentenceScript(), which give 4 and 2 on v<=2 and the variables' values otherwise. On v1-v2 a waiting
message is the bare opcode 0xAE (o2_waitForMessage), '.' is on when VAR_TALKSTOP_KEY is 0xFF (the engine's own gate),
and a running global 4 is no idle blocker by itself (each click restarts it; MM's hover loop on one verb).

The v1-v2 verb screen draws more than the verb slots. uiSlots() lists, after them (slots from _numVerbs, ids from 256):
the sentence line (id 256, named by the ids in the four sentence variables, while it is drawn), the inventory boxes that
show an object (ids 257-260, named "#" and the object's id, the image verbs' convention) and the scroll arrows whose
click turns a page (261, 262). stateJson, stateLiteJson, wireObs and wireBlock list them; hitSlot(), used by the "at"
reply, wireAt and the input log, answers ScummEngine_v2::checkExecVerbs()'s order read-only (never checkV2Inventory(),
which scrolls): 0 on the sentence line (a click there runs no verb), a box's or an arrow's slot. Actor and ego
positions use getPos() and the elevation is scaled to pixels on v1-v2 (getPos() is getRealPos() on v3 and later).
No pixel and no game text leaves the process.

Every change is inside a version <= 2 branch or gives the same values on v3 and later: Monkey Island's and the Fate of
Atlantis demo's free runs (frames.jsonl, trace.jsonl, state-start.json) are byte-identical.

On top of patches 0001-0011 (the tree of svm-e027); the engine built with it is svm-e028.

